## 1. The Big Idea

_Athleticism is a **complete instrument cluster** — four banks of gauges (Chassis, Engine, Outputs, Control), each needle reading **you against a redline target** — and the whole panel is driven by a **four-position annual dial** that builds one bank while the rest idle at maintenance. The poster is the master control board an engineer would mount to read an entire machine at a glance: the **gaps between needle and redline are the diagnosis** (where the engine has missing parts), the **block-cycle dial is the plan** (build one, hold three, swap, repeat yearly), and a small **idle-power readout** delivers the punchline — once built, the entire panel holds on ~3–4 hrs/week. The reader's takeaway lands in the geometry: athleticism is a panel you read, not a number you chase, and the year is one full turn of the dial._

## 2. Visual Metaphor & Structure

A **master instrument cluster + annual block-cycle dial.** Three stacked instrument zones, read top→down, with Zone 1 dominant — it *is* the "assembled machine" payoff of the whole series.

**ZONE 1 — THE MASTER CLUSTER (the standard; the hero).**
A full control board carrying **four labeled gauge banks**, each bank a clear sub-panel with its own header. Every gauge shows the same honest format: a **field-test label**, a **redline target tick (men / women)**, and a **"you" needle** with the gap between needle and redline left visible. The four banks, left→right / top→down:

- **BANK 1 — CHASSIS** (`look + force`): `Bench 1.5× / 1.0× BW` · `Deadlift 2.0× / 1.5× BW` · `Squat 1.75× / 1.25× BW` · `Body fat 10–14% / 18–22%` · `FFMI 20–23`.
- **BANK 2 — ENGINE** (`the motor that buys years`): `VO₂ max 52+ / 45+` · `1.5-mile <10:30 / <12:00` · `decoupling <5% drift`.
- **BANK 3 — OUTPUTS** (`expression`): `push-ups 60+ / 40+` · `pull-ups 10+ / 5+` · `vertical 24" / 18"` · `broad jump >8' / >6.5'` · `5-10-5 <4.5 / <5.0 s` · `ruler-drop <15 cm`.
- **BANK 4 — CONTROL** (`move + last`): `sit-and-reach >15 cm` · `single-leg eyes-closed >60 s` · `tennis-wall rally 50+`.

The whole-cluster caption, the article's core idea: ==`the gaps are the diagnosis — the spread of what you can't do tells you which lever to pull.`== A single small annotation pins the honest timeline: `2–3 yrs of consistent, intelligent work to hit most lines as a non-elite athlete.`

**ZONE 2 — THE ANNUAL BLOCK-CYCLE DIAL (the plan / the "how").**
A **four-sector rotary dial** (a quarter each), one sector illuminated **BUILD** and the other three dimmed to **HOLD** — visually encoding "you can only max one bank at a time." Reading clockwise:

- **Q1 — GPP / FOUNDATION** → builds *Engine + Outputs base* (`4× Zone 2 · 1 work-capacity · full-body moderate · daily CARs`).
- **Q2 — STRENGTH / CHASSIS** → builds *Chassis* (`4× heavy progression · cardio at MAINTENANCE`).
- **Q3 — ENGINE / CEILING** → builds *Engine* (`4× Zone 2 + 2× hard intervals · lifting at MAINTENANCE`).
- **Q4 — POWER / INTEGRATION** → builds *Outputs* (`jumps · sprints · reactive drills · contrast lifting · retest the full battery`).

A center hub label ties it together: ==`BUILD ONE BANK · HOLD THE REST · SWAP · repeat yearly — the slope keeps climbing for years.`== A thin arrow on the dial rim shows the rotation direction and that it loops back to Q1.

**ZONE 3 — THE IDLE-POWER READOUT + THE DIVIDEND (the punchline / the "why it's worth it").**
A small, set-apart **"maintenance idle" meter** — the surprise payoff: `HOLD THE WHOLE PANEL ≈ 3–4 hrs / wk` with two sub-readouts `VO₂ max held ≈ 3 × 30 min/wk (intensity, not volume)` and `strength held ≈ 2 hard sets / muscle / wk @ 0–1 RIR`. Caption: ==`build hard once — then hold easily, for decades.`==

Beneath it, a quiet two-line **dividend footer** (the emotional close, deliberately understated, not a gauge): `LONGEVITY — CRF vs all-cause mortality: no upper limit of benefit (Mandsager 2018, n=122,007).` · `AVAILABILITY — a body that does what you ask changes how you walk through the world.`

This sub-archetype — **four-bank master gauge cluster → four-sector annual block dial → idle-power maintenance readout → dividend footer** — is unmistakably "Engineering Diagnostic Instrument" and is the *fullest, most assembled* instrument in the Fit set, which is exactly right for the synthesis poster.

## 3. Layout — exact composition

**Orientation: portrait** (~3:4 or 4:5, poster / blog-hero friendly). Eye path is a strong top→down read: take in the assembled panel, then the dial that drives it, then the small payoff at the bottom.

- **Top band (~8%) — MASTER HEADLINE.** Lockup: **"THE WHOLE PANEL."** sub: *athleticism is four banks of gauges. The gaps are the map. One year is one turn of the dial.*
- **Upper-to-mid band (~46%) — THE MASTER CLUSTER.** Dominant. The four gauge banks arranged as a 2×2 of sub-panels (Chassis top-left, Engine top-right, Outputs bottom-left, Control bottom-right) **or** four stacked horizontal banks if portrait gets tight. Each bank is clearly bordered, headed, and carries its gauges with the `target ▸ you ▸ gap` format. The "gaps are the diagnosis" caption runs under the whole cluster. This zone is the brightest, busiest beat — the "assembled machine."
- **Mid-to-lower band (~30%) — THE ANNUAL DIAL.** The four-sector rotary, centered, with Q-by-Q build/hold labels around the rim and the "build one, hold three, swap" hub note. The one lit BUILD sector is the highest-contrast element in this zone.
- **Lower band (~10%) — IDLE-POWER READOUT.** The small maintenance meter, set apart (boxed / lower-right), with the "build hard once, hold easily" caption — the deliberate surprise.
- **Footer band (~6%) — DIVIDEND.** Two quiet lines (longevity + availability). No gauge, no chrome — the human note that closes the series.

Visual hierarchy, largest→smallest: (1) the MASTER CLUSTER as a whole and the visible needle-to-redline **gaps**, (2) the BUILD-lit sector of the ANNUAL DIAL, (3) the rest of the dial / its rotation, (4) the IDLE-POWER readout, (5) the dividend footer.

